#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""satnogs-worker — host-side processing of archived SatNOGS IQ recordings.

satnogs-post (inside the container) archives each pass as <obs>.sigmf-data +
<obs>.sigmf-meta and touches queue/<obs>. This worker, run from a systemd
timer on the host, takes each queued observation and:

  1. finds transmission bursts (cheap, band-limited energy detector)
  2. sets the sample rate from the flowgraph rule (exact) and measures the
     satellite's true baud from its symbol clock (history fallback when weak)
  3. measures each burst: SNR, Eb/N0, frequency offset, occupied bandwidth
     -> SigMF annotations
  4. no bursts -> status "empty", no decode (unless always_decode)
  5. decodes with gr-satellites (built-in name, NORAD ID, or SatYAML file)
  6. parses frames into telemetry (satnogs-decoders or own Kaitai parser)
  7. stores everything in SQLite and writes core:sample_rate, status and
     annotations back into the .sigmf-meta

Usage:
  satnogs-worker [options] run [--max N]        process the queue
  satnogs-worker [options] reprocess OBS_ID...  redo specific observations
  satnogs-worker [options] status               queue / database summary

Options: --base DIR  --config FILE  --db FILE  -v
"""
